        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Species: Cortinarius kioloensis\n- Places: Higgins Creek, Kioloa State Forest, Batemans Bay, southern New South Wales, South Coast region, Australia, Deua National Park, Moruya, Narooma\n\nFacts:\n- The type specimen of Cortinarius kioloensis was collected along Higgins Creek in Kioloa State Forest near Batemans Bay in southern New South Wales on 22 June 1980.\n- Batemans Bay is a town in the South Coast region of New South Wales, Australia.\n- The nearest coastal towns to Deua National Park are Batemans Bay, Moruya, and Narooma.",
